<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?><rss version="2.0"><channel><title>PRESS RELEASES FROM RBI</title><link>http://www.rbi.org.in</link><description>This is Feed from RBI for Press Releases.</description><copyright>Copyright Reserve Bank of India. All Rights Reserved.</copyright><item><title><![CDATA[Reporting of FCNR(B) Deposits, External Commercial Borrowings (ECBs) and Overseas Foreign Currency Borrowings (OFCBs) mobilized under Reserve Bank’s Swap Facility]]></title><description><![CDATA[<table width="100%" border="0" align="center" class="td">  <tr>    <td><p>RBI had announced a facility for offering concessional swaps for fresh FCNR(B) deposits, OFCB and ECB inflows, on June 05, 2026 and the same was operationalised on June 08, 2026, which is available upto September 30, 2026, for the FCNR(B) deposits and upto December 31, 2026, for the OFCBs and ECBs.</p>    <p>Based on the data received from Authorised Dealer Banks, the position of forex inflows mobilised till July 31, 2026, under the above facility is given below.</p>    <table width="70%" border="0" align="center" cellpadding="0" cellspacing="1" class="tablebg">      <tr class="head">        <td width="50%" align="center">Type</td>        <td width="50%" align="center">Amount<br>          (USD million)</td>      </tr>      <tr>        <td>FCNR(B) Deposits</td>        <td align="right">36,725</td>      </tr>      <tr>        <td>OFCBs</td>        <td align="right">2,575</td>      </tr>      <tr>        <td>ECBs</td>        <td align="right">1,516</td>      </tr>      <tr>        <td>Total</td>        <td align="right">40,816</td>      </tr>    </table><p align="right"><span class="head">(Brij Raj)</span>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<br>  Chief General Manager</p><p class="head">Press Release: 2026-2027/796</p></td>  </tr></table>]]></description><link>https://www.rbi.org.in/scripts/BS_PressReleaseDisplay.aspx?prid=63274</link><pubDate>Sat, 01 Aug 2026 09:45:00</pubDate></item><item><title><![CDATA[Auction of State Government Securities]]></title><description><![CDATA[<table width="100%" border="0" align="center" class="td">  <tr>    <td><p>The following State Governments have offered to sell stock by way of auction, for an aggregate amount of <span class="head">&#8377;26,850 Crore</span> (Face Value). </p>      <table width="95%" border="0" align="center" cellpadding="0" cellspacing="1" class="tablebg">        <tr class="head">          <td width="6%" align="center">Sr. No.</td>          <td width="19%" align="center">State/UT</td>          <td width="15%" align="center">Amount to be raised<br>            (&#8377; Crore)</td>          <td width="47%" align="center">Tenor <br>          (Year)</td>          <td width="13%" align="center">Type of Auction</td>        </tr>        <tr>          <td align="center" valign="top">1.</td>          <td valign="top">Assam</td>          <td align="right" valign="top">1000</td>          <td align="right" valign="top">Re-issue of 7.56% Assam SGS 2036, issued on July 22, 2026</td>          <td align="right" valign="top">Price</td>        </tr>        <tr>          <td rowspan="2" align="center" valign="top">2.</td>          <td rowspan="2" valign="top">Bihar</td>          <td align="right" valign="top">800</td>          <td align="right" valign="top">Re-issue of 7.42% Bihar SGS 2035, issued on July 08, 2026</td>          <td align="right" valign="top">Price</td>        </tr>        <tr>          <td align="right" valign="top">1200</td>          <td align="right" valign="top">Re-issue of 7.92% Bihar SGS 2051, issued on April 15, 2026</td>          <td align="right" valign="top">Price</td>        </tr>        <tr>          <td rowspan="2" align="center" valign="top">3.</td>          <td rowspan="2" valign="top">Chhattisgarh</td>          <td align="right" valign="top">500</td>          <td align="right" valign="top">Re-issue of 7.40% Chhattisgarh SGS 2035, issued on July 08, 2026</td>          <td align="right" valign="top">Price</td>        </tr>        <tr>          <td align="right" valign="top">500</td>          <td align="right" valign="top">Re-issue of 7.64% Chhattisgarh SGS 2042, issued on July 08, 2026</td>          <td align="right" valign="top">Price</td>        </tr>        <tr>          <td rowspan="2" align="center" valign="top">4.</td>          <td rowspan="2" valign="top">Gujarat</td>          <td align="right" valign="top">1000</td>          <td align="right" valign="top">Re-issue of 7.38% Gujarat SGS 2035, issued on July 15, 2026</td>          <td align="right" valign="top">Price</td>        </tr>        <tr>          <td align="right" valign="top">1500</td>          <td align="right" valign="top">Re-issue of 7.51% Gujarat SGS 2038, issued on July 15, 2026</td>          <td align="right" valign="top">Price</td>        </tr>        <tr>          <td rowspan="2" align="center" valign="top">5.</td>          <td rowspan="2" valign="top">Himachal Pradesh</td>          <td align="right" valign="top">400</td>          <td align="right" valign="top">Re-issue of 7.78% Himachal Pradesh SGS 2044, issued on June 24, 2026</td>          <td align="right" valign="top">Price</td>        </tr>        <tr>          <td align="right" valign="top">300</td>          <td align="right" valign="top">Re-issue of 7.77% Himachal Pradesh SGS 2049, issued on June 24, 2026</td>          <td align="right" valign="top">Price</td>        </tr>        <tr>          <td rowspan="2" align="center" valign="top">6.</td>          <td rowspan="2" valign="top">Jammu and Kashmir</td>          <td align="right" valign="top">500</td>          <td align="right" valign="top">Re-issue of 7.91% Jammu and Kashmir SGS 2046, issued on June 03, 2026</td>          <td align="right" valign="top">Price</td>        </tr>        <tr>          <td align="right" valign="top">500</td>          <td align="right" valign="top">Re-issue of 7.81% Jammu and Kashmir SGS 2051, issued on June 10, 2026</td>          <td align="right" valign="top">Price</td>        </tr>        <tr>          <td align="center" valign="top">7.</td>          <td valign="top">Jharkhand</td>          <td align="right" valign="top">1000</td>          <td align="right" valign="top">Re-issue of 7.30% Jharkhand SGS 2033, issued on July 08, 2026</td>          <td align="right" valign="top">Price</td>        </tr>        <tr>          <td rowspan="2" align="center" valign="top">8.</td>          <td rowspan="2" valign="top">Kerala</td>          <td align="right" valign="top">800</td>          <td align="right" valign="top">Re-issue of 7.30% Kerala SGS 2033, issued on July 08, 2026</td>          <td align="right" valign="top">Price</td>        </tr>        <tr>          <td align="right" valign="top">1000</td>          <td align="right" valign="top">Re-issue of 7.56% Kerala SGS 2039, issued on July 08, 2026</td>          <td align="right" valign="top">Price</td>        </tr>        <tr>          <td rowspan="2" align="center" valign="top">9.</td>          <td rowspan="2" valign="top">Madhya Pradesh</td>          <td align="right" valign="top">1600</td>          <td align="right" valign="top">Re-issue of 7.61% Madhya Pradesh SGS 2044, issued on July 08, 2026</td>          <td align="right" valign="top">Price</td>        </tr>        <tr>          <td align="right" valign="top">2000</td>          <td align="right" valign="top">Re-issue of 7.90% Madhya Pradesh SGS 2056, issued on April 15, 2026</td>          <td align="right" valign="top">Price</td>        </tr>        <tr>          <td align="center" valign="top">10.</td>          <td valign="top">Manipur</td>          <td align="right" valign="top">250</td>          <td align="right" valign="top">Re-issue of 7.64% Manipur SGS 2040, issued on July 08, 2026</td>          <td align="right" valign="top">Price</td>        </tr>        <tr>          <td rowspan="2" align="center" valign="top">11.</td>          <td rowspan="2" valign="top">Odisha</td>          <td align="right" valign="top">1000</td>          <td align="right" valign="top">04</td>          <td align="right" valign="top">Yield</td>        </tr>        <tr>          <td align="right" valign="top">1000</td>          <td align="right" valign="top">14</td>          <td align="right" valign="top">Yield</td>        </tr>        <tr>          <td align="center" valign="top">12.</td>          <td valign="top">Sikkim</td>          <td align="right" valign="top">200</td>          <td align="right" valign="top">Re-issue of 7.58% Sikkim SGS 2039, issued on July 08, 2026</td>          <td align="right" valign="top">Price</td>        </tr>        <tr>          <td rowspan="3" align="center" valign="top">13.</td>          <td rowspan="3" valign="top">Tamil Nadu</td>          <td align="right" valign="top">1000</td>          <td align="right" valign="top">10</td>          <td align="right" valign="top">Yield</td>        </tr>        <tr>          <td align="right" valign="top">1000</td>          <td align="right" valign="top">15</td>          <td align="right" valign="top">Yield</td>        </tr>        <tr>          <td align="right" valign="top">500</td>          <td align="right" valign="top">25</td>          <td align="right" valign="top">Yield</td>        </tr>        <tr>          <td rowspan="4" align="center" valign="top">14.</td>          <td rowspan="4" valign="top">Telangana</td>          <td align="right" valign="top">500</td>          <td align="right" valign="top">Re-issue of 7.53% Telangana SGS 2039, issued on July 01, 2026</td>          <td align="right" valign="top">Price</td>        </tr>        <tr>          <td align="right" valign="top">500</td>          <td align="right" valign="top">Re-issue of 7.64% Telangana SGS 2044, issued on July 01, 2026</td>          <td align="right" valign="top">Price</td>        </tr>        <tr>          <td align="right" valign="top">500</td>          <td align="right" valign="top">Re-issue of 7.65% Telangana SGS 2049, issued on July 01, 2026</td>          <td align="right" valign="top">Price</td>        </tr>        <tr>          <td align="right" valign="top">1000</td>          <td align="right" valign="top">Re-issue of 7.65% Telangana SGS 2055, issued on July 01, 2026</td>          <td align="right" valign="top">Price</td>        </tr>        <tr>          <td rowspan="3" align="center" valign="top">15.</td>          <td rowspan="3" valign="top">Uttar Pradesh</td>          <td align="right" valign="top">1000</td>          <td align="right" valign="top">Re-issue of 7.14% Uttar Pradesh SGS 2032, issued on July 08, 2026</td>          <td align="right" valign="top">Price</td>        </tr>        <tr>          <td align="right" valign="top">1000</td>          <td align="right" valign="top">Re-issue of 7.59% Uttar Pradesh SGS 2042, issued on July 08, 2026</td>          <td align="right" valign="top">Price</td>        </tr>        <tr>          <td align="right" valign="top">1000</td>          <td align="right" valign="top">Re-issue of 7.79% Uttar Pradesh SGS 2051, issued on March 25, 2026</td>          <td align="right" valign="top">Price</td>        </tr>        <tr>          <td align="center" valign="top">16.</td>          <td valign="top">Uttarakhand</td>          <td align="right" valign="top">300</td>          <td align="right" valign="top">12</td>          <td align="right" valign="top">Yield</td>        </tr>        <tr>          <td rowspan="3" align="center" valign="top">17.</td>          <td rowspan="3" valign="top">West Bengal</td>          <td align="right" valign="top">500</td>          <td align="right" valign="top">Re-issue of 7.07% West Bengal SGS 2031, issued on July 08, 2026</td>          <td align="right" valign="top">Price</td>        </tr>        <tr>          <td align="right" valign="top">500</td>          <td align="right" valign="top">Re-issue of 7.64% West Bengal SGS 2044, issued on July 08, 2026</td>          <td align="right" valign="top">Price</td>        </tr>        <tr>          <td align="right" valign="top">500</td>          <td align="right" valign="top">Re-issue of 7.65% West Bengal SGS 2052, issued on July 08, 2026</td>          <td align="right" valign="top">Price</td>        </tr>        <tr>          <td valign="top">&nbsp;</td>          <td valign="top">Total</td>          <td align="right" valign="top"> 26850</td>          <td valign="top">&nbsp;</td>          <td valign="top">&nbsp;</td>        </tr>      </table>      <p>The auction will be conducted on the Reserve Bank of India Core Banking Solution (E-Kuber) system on <span class="head">August 04, 2026 (Tuesday)</span>. The Government Stock up to ten per cent of the notified amount of the sale of each stock will be allotted to eligible individuals and institutions, subject to a maximum limit of one per cent of its notified amount for a single bid per stock as per the &lsquo;<a href="https://www.rbi.org.in/Scripts/NotificationUser.aspx?Id=11725&Mode=0" target="_blank" class="links">Scheme for Non-competitive Bidding Facility</a>&rsquo;. Individual investors can also place bids as per the non-competitive scheme through the Retail Direct portal (<a href="https://rbiretaildirect.org.in" target="_blank" class="links">https://rbiretaildirect.org.in</a>).</p>      <p>Both competitive and non-competitive bids for the auction should be submitted in electronic format on the Reserve Bank of India Core Banking Solution (E-Kuber) system on <u class="head">August 04, 2026 (Tuesday). The competitive bids should be submitted between 10:30 A.M. and 11:30 A.M. and non-competitive bids should be submitted between 10:30 A.M. and 11:00 A.M.</u></p>      <p>In case of technical difficulties, Core Banking Operations Team may be contacted (<a href="mailto:cbot@rbi.org.in" class="links">email</a>; Phone no: 022-69870466, 022-69870415).</p>      <p>For other auction related difficulties, IDMD Auction Team can be contacted (<a href="mailto:auctionidmd@rbi.org.in" class="links">email</a>; Phone no: 022-22702431, 022-22705125).</p>      <p>Only in the event of system failure, physical bids would be accepted. Such physical bids should be submitted to the Public Debt Office (<a href="mailto:bids@rbi.org.in" class="links">email</a>; Phone no: 022-22603456, 022-22603457, 022-22603190) in the prescribed form obtainable from RBI website (<a href="https://www.rbi.org.in/Scripts/BS_ViewForms.aspx" target="_blank" class="links">https://www.rbi.org.in/Scripts/BS_ViewForms.aspx</a>) before the auction timing ends.</p>      <p>The yield per cent per annum or the price as the case may be, expected by the bidder should be expressed up to two decimal points. An investor can submit more than one competitive bid at same/different rates of yield or prices in electronic format on the Reserve Bank of India Core Banking Solution (E-Kuber) system. However, the aggregate amount of bids submitted by a bidder should not exceed the notified amount for each State.</p>      <p>The Reserve Bank of India will determine the maximum yield / minimum price at which bids will be accepted. Stock will be issued for a minimum nominal amount of &#8377;10,000.00 and in multiples of &#8377;10,000.00 thereafter.</p>      <p>The results of the auction will be announced on <span class="head">August 04, 2026 (Tuesday)</span> and payment by successful bidders will be made during banking hours on <span class="head">August 05, 2026 (Wednesday)</span> at Mumbai and at respective Regional Offices of RBI.</p>      <p>The new State Government Stocks will bear interest at the rates determined by RBI at the auctions. For the <span class="head">new stock</span>, interest will be paid half yearly on <span class="head">February 05</span> and <span class="head">August 05</span> of each year till maturity. For the re-issued Government Stock, interest will be paid at the rate as determined on the date of original issue of Government Stock and will be paid on half yearly basis till maturity. The Stocks will be governed by the provisions of the Government Securities Act, 2006 and the Government Securities Regulations, 2007.</p>      <p>The investment in State Government Stocks will be reckoned as an eligible investment in Government Securities by banks for the purpose of Statutory Liquidity Ratio (SLR) under Section 24 of the Banking Regulation Act, 1949. The stocks will qualify for the ready forward facility.</p>      <p align="right"><span class="head">Ajit Prasad&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</span><br aria-hidden="true">        Deputy General Manager<br aria-hidden="true">        (Communications)&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</p>    <p class="head">Press Release: 2026-2027/795</p></td>  </tr></table>]]></description><link>https://www.rbi.org.in/scripts/BS_PressReleaseDisplay.aspx?prid=63273</link><pubDate>Fri, 31 Jul 2026 19:35:00</pubDate></item><item><title><![CDATA[Buyback of Government of India Dated Securities]]></title><description><![CDATA[<table width="100%" border="0" align="center" class="td"><tr>  <td><p>The Government of India has announced the buyback of its Securities through auction for an aggregate amount of <span class="head">&#8377;20,000 crore</span> (face value). The security-wise details of the buyback are as under:</p>      <table width="85%" border="0" align="center" cellpadding="0" cellspacing="1" class="tablebg">        <tr class="head">          <td width="10%" align="center">S.No.</td>          <td width="45%" align="center">Security</td>          <td width="45%" align="center">Date of Maturity</td>        </tr>        <tr>          <td align="center">1.</td>          <td>7.33% GS 2026 </td>          <td>October 30, 2026 </td>        </tr>        <tr>          <td align="center">2.</td>          <td>5.74% GS 2026 </td>          <td>November 15, 2026 </td>        </tr>        <tr>          <td align="center">3.</td>          <td>8.15% GS 2026 </td>          <td>November 24, 2026 </td>        </tr>        <tr>          <td align="center">4.</td>          <td>8.24% GS 2027 </td>          <td>February 15, 2027 </td>        </tr>      </table>      <p>There is no notified amount for the individual securities within the aggregate ceiling of &#8377;20,000 crore. Auction for securities will be conducted using multiple price method. The offers for the auction should be submitted in electronic format on the Reserve Bank of India Core Banking Solution (E-Kuber) system on <span class="head">August 06, 2026</span> (Thursday) between <span class="head">10:30 a.m. and 11:30 a.m</span>. The result of the auction will be announced on the same day and settlement will take place on <span class="head">August 07, 2026</span> (Friday).</p>      <p>Government of India reserves the right to:</p>      <ul>        <li>          <p>Decide on the quantum of buyback of individual securities.</p>        </li>        <li>          <p>Accept more or less than the notified amount of &#8377;20,000 crore.</p>        </li>        <li>          <p>        Accept or reject any or all of the offers, either wholly or partially, without assigning any reason thereof. </p>        </li>      </ul>      <p align="right"><span class="head">(Brij Raj)</span>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<br aria-hidden="true">Chief General Manager</p>      <p class="head">Press Release: 2026-2027/794</p></td></tr></table>]]></description><link>https://www.rbi.org.in/scripts/BS_PressReleaseDisplay.aspx?prid=63272</link><pubDate>Fri, 31 Jul 2026 18:00:00</pubDate></item></channel></rss>